# ============================================================
# Powder XRD pattern -- 2-theta / intensity, 2 columns.
# ============================================================
# This is the CANONICAL model stb-xrdrank's --experimental (and stb-xrd's
# --compare-to, same core/xrd.py::read_experimental_pattern reader) expects:
#   column 1 = 2theta (degrees)
#   column 2 = intensity (any scale -- both sides get max-normalized before
#              comparing, so 0-100, 0-1, raw counts, whatever your source
#              uses is all fine)
# Whitespace- OR comma-separated. Blank lines and '#' comments (like this
# whole header) are skipped. See examples/4.6-xrd/README.md section 3.4 for
# what happens with a 3rd (or more) column, and why it matters.
#
# Real data, not fabricated: this is bulk silicon (diamond cubic, Fd-3m),
# Cu-K-alpha (1.54184 Ang), 2theta = 1-120 deg, 0.01 deg step -- the exact
# same file used in this session's own real /home/carlos/test/Si analysis
# (README section 5), with its original (always-zero, unused) 3rd column
# removed so this file is the clean, minimal, correct model to copy.
# ============================================================
